---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About | Ursa fab."
  description="Meet Ursa fab., an independent Norwich workshop producing high-end metalwork and bespoke fabrication for creative clients, homes and small businesses."
  image="/about.jpeg"
>
  <Header alwaysVisible />

  <main class="content-page">
    <section class="content-media">
      <div class="content-hero">
        <img src="/about.jpeg" alt="Ursa fab. workshop" />
      </div>

      <p class="content-label-about"><b>THE CRAFTING BEAR</b> - <em>Ursus fabricatoris f. difficilis</em></p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-copy">
      <h1>Ursa fab. - handcrafted in Norwich, UK.</h1>

      <p>
        Existing at the juncture between garage industry and large-scale fabrication, 
        we aim to make high-end metalcraft as accessible as possible to artists, 
        creatives, homes, and small businesses. 
        Whether you have a fully-fledged  design, a sketch of an idea, or just a 
        problem to solve, we can make your projects a reality in almost any material - 
        using the best possible manual welding and machining equipment, precision 
        fixturing, in-house design and selected supply partners.
      </p>
      <br/>
      <br/>
      <hr/>
      <br/>

      <p>
        Ursa fab. is the professional expression of myself, Tom van Baalen - 
        a resident of Norwich since 2008, studying at the University of East Anglia. 
        Grown from a love of traditional crafts, heritage industry, and the natural world 
        beyond and behind us; it is, I hope, a vehicle to make long-lasting and 
        beautiful things for the people that appreciate them.
      </p>

      <p> 
        Leaving a past life in fields and laboratories as a technician, 
        I seized an opportunity to retrain as a metalworker, 
        and I have been incredibly lucky to learn from some extraordinary colleagues and friends. 
        From a crash course in all the fundamentals of materials prep, design, machining, welding and finishing 
        in the workshop of Sam Fish 
        (an enormously skilled and patient craftsperson to whom I am forever indebted), 
        I dove into the deep end of the welding and fabrication industry,
        primarily working on sports car subframes and fuel tanks,
        and honing my skills on stainless steel hygenic fixtures and fittings.
        Surfacing on the other side to start my own workshop in spring of 2024, I now follow my own path 
        making things that are, I hope, interesting, creative and wanted.
      </p>

    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
